/-!
# Valuation bound for E(σ_γ z) under a non-zero limit

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.LevelN.valuation_apply_smul_le_one_of_tendsto_div_smul`
(`4f16a8a0-3d21-586e-89f5-b1dda8087576`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `bde924d6-51e1-5e64-99c4-7c7e87058e72`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix $M \ge 1$ and let $A_M =$ [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
M`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) be the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of functions
$\mathcal{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by $j = E_4^3/\Delta$ together with the functions `fricke M
v` for the non-zero $v \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^2$. Let $K$ be a field that is a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and
an $A_M$-algebra compatibly, and a fraction field of $A_M$. Assume $A_M$ is stable under right
translation, i.e. $F \circ \gamma \in A_M$ for all $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $F \in
A_M$; let $\sigma \colon \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{C}}(K)$ be a monoid
homomorphism acting on $A_M$ by $\sigma_\gamma(F) = F \circ \gamma^{-1}$, and let $E \colon K \to
\mathbb{C}((q))$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra map with $E(j)$ equal to the image under $q \mapsto
q_M^{M}$ (exponents multiplied by $M$) of $q^{-1}$ times the power series $\mathrm{eisenstein4}^3
\cdot \mathrm{dedekindEtaUnitInv}$ over $\mathbb{C}$, and with $E(F) \cdot \widetilde{\Delta}^m$
equal to the level-$M$ $q$-expansion of $F\Delta^m$ whenever $F \in A_M$, $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and $F
\Delta^m$ is bounded at $i\infty$, where $\widetilde{\Delta}$ is the level-$M$ $q$-expansion of
$\Delta$. Let $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ be of finite index with $\Gamma(M) \le \Gamma$
and $T \in \Gamma$, let $g, h$ be modular forms of weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ for $\Gamma$ with $h
\neq 0$, and let $z \in K$ satisfy $E(z) \cdot \tilde{h}(q_M^M) = \tilde{g}(q_M^M)$, where
$\tilde{g}, \tilde{h}$ are the level-$1$ $q$-expansions of $g, h$. Then for $\gamma \in
\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $L \neq 0$ such that $g(\gamma^{-1}\tau)/h(\gamma^{-1}\tau) \to L$ as
$\operatorname{Im}\tau \to \infty$, the Laurent series $E(\sigma_\gamma z)$ has valuation at most
$1$, i.e. non-negative order in $\mathbb{C}((q_M))$.

This is the analytic input, cusp by cusp, to the statement that a quotient $g/h$ of modular forms
with finite non-zero limit at the cusp $\gamma^{-1}(i\infty)$ has no pole there: the element of the
function field $K$ realising $g/h$ has $q$-expansion without polar terms after applying
$\sigma_\gamma$. It is used by
[`ModularCurve.ord_eq_zero_of_not_mem_of_realizeOf_tendsto`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_eq_zero_of_not_mem_of_realizeOf_tendsto).

